  "name": "Apolipoprotein A1 (APO-A1)",
  "code": "APOA1",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Apo A1 Level (mg/dL)</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Below Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Low Apo A1 levels may be associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases, such as coronary artery disease. Low levels may also indicate certain lipid metabolism disorders. Further evaluation is necessary to identify the underlying cause and appropriate management.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Apo A1 levels within the normal range are considered to be optimal for cardiovascular health and lipid metabolism.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Above Normal Range</div></td><td><div>High Apo A1 levels are generally considered beneficial for cardiovascular health and may indicate a reduced risk of heart disease. However, extremely high levels may require further evaluation to rule out any underlying conditions.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
